Keep one ticket per supported cause, not one ticket per subject line.
The [review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-review) shows why the distinction matters.

## The rule

[Decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) replaces the subject-only rule in
[decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject). Keep that accepted record unchanged.

1. Deduplicate exported rows by report ID.
2. Read the body and resolve the tenant's locale, form version and report channel.
3. Compare supported causes with `causeOf` and `sameCause`, not subject text.
4. Merge only known, matching causes. Keep unknown or conflicting cases for investigation.
5. Keep each report's ID and the count with its engineering ticket.

<Callout>
Different subjects can describe the same cause. Matching subjects can describe different causes.
Browser locale and intake tags are not substitutes for the tenant directory.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Do not assume a duplicate. Get tenant details and compare symptoms and evidence.
The five timing notes in the incident review remain visible within the supplied parser group
until investigation supports a different classification.

## Maintenance

Rebuild from each new desk export and review the page when the evidence changes.
A ticket marked known, merged, or queued is not proof of a verified fix.

